  matters referred to the executive  reports from other committees  there are none so to the main event of  the evening which is  agenda item number seven provisional  financial out turn  the portfolio holder for financial  services council simon smith will  present the report council smith  thank you chairman um before i get  started i'd  just like to take the opportunity to  thank  naomi and her team for all the work  that has gone into this it's condensed  into a  a small report but it should know me by  no means uh  take away from the sheer quantity of  work that goes into  preparing our financial figures  i've got a number of uh points that i  i'll talk you through  the original general fund revenue budget  was 9.8 million  the provisional outrun was 10.3 million  which is unfavorable variance of 0.5  million  in addition to the original base budget  one million pound of  drawdowns from reserves was approved for  specific purposes  during the year and these are detailed  in appendix 2.  it's requested to carry forward 1.4  million of budget  relating to specific projects grant  funded expenditure  on one-off items including 0.5 million  of sales fees and charges  compensation grant income into 2122  as detailed in appendices 4a and 4b  once these items are accounted for the  overall overspend  rises to 0.9 million the  this underlying overspend reflects the  impact of cobit 19 on service budget  areas  to help mitigate these these pressures  the government provided the council with  a coveted 19  general grant allocation of 1.1 million  application of this grant reduces the  net position  to 8.2 million underspend which is a  small increase of sixty thousand pounds  compared to the position reported to the  executive  in quarter three back in february  as well as the general kobit nineteen  grand the government has also provided  several of the specific  covid19 grand allegations which are  reported separately  the details of these can be found in the  table at appendix  4c the capital programme  totaling 2.9 million  was approved at full council in february  2020.  the executive agreed to reprofile this  in quarter one  giving a revised capital budget of 1.9  million  the provisional outrun capital outrun  position  is 1.2 million as set out in appendix 5.  this includes 0.5 million of slippage on  projects  mainly due to cobit 19 delaying  completion of works  this is requested to be carried forward  into 21-22  the council holds sufficient reserves  and balances to support the long-term  longer-term financial stability of the  council  although it should be noted that the  majority of these reserves  are earmarked for specific purposes and  will not be available  unless decisions are taken to reconsider  the council's strategic priorities  and associate other associated funding  commitments  the reserve's position is detailed at  appendix  3. to summarise the report shows that  despite the adverse impacts of cobit 19  on the council's budgets  additional grant funding combined with  savings on salaries  and other budgets has meant that the  council has been able to contain its  pressures  in the short term and deliver against  its corporate priorities  while maintaining its planned  contributions to reserves  for projects such as the connect program  program  however the covid 19 losses and cost  pressures experienced in 2021  are continuing into twenty one twenty  two  and may extend into the medium term  the government's income compensation  scheme will  continue for the first quarter of 21 22  and some additional grant support has  been made available  for this financial year however the  council  is likely to have to take difficult  decisions  to ensure its financial sustainability  in the median term  unless additional ongoing resources are  planned  are agreed for local authorities as part  of the  comprehensive spending review which is  planned in 2021  chairman you can't say by any means  that last year was a good year last year  was a terrible year  in all sorts of ways but in terms of the  way in which we've  managed our budget i do believe we have  we have performed as well as we possibly  could given all the circumstances  and so therefore i ask the executive to  recommend  to approve the recommendations to set  out on the 10 points  in section 1 of the report thank you  thank you councillor smith  are there any questions at this stage  for either councillor smith  or for him to delegate and ask naomi  lucas to  help us out any questions members  council award thank you chairman it's  just an observation  that at how well we have done in  consideration  of the shocking period that we've had  it is a great credit i think to  everybody  who works and is part of locksmith  district council  that we've actually got ourselves  through what could have been  an awful financial mess  that we've come out this way it's it's  amazing to be quite honest and  i have to say i have to be very proud to  be a member of this executive in this  council  that has worked so well to actually  achieve and  give credit to the portfolio holder and  naomi and her staff  in what's going on but not only that to  all the ladies  and the acting manager director because  you know we've had to  ban some enormous costs and we've got  through it  and i have to applaud them thank you  counselor  thank you very much indeed any other  comments from members  no i wish to uh make a few points before  the girl's recommendations and council  award  uh you and i didn't speak before this  meeting but you could have stolen  my speech but nevertheless so i'm  actually going to say  much for saying that under the  stewardship of portfolio holder  simon smith we have been fortunate to be  able to steer a ship  politically in an extremely sound  way and i like you i'm extremely proud  to be  the leader of this council at this time  it will be a very difficult time  but i also want to pay tribute to naomi  lucas who steers the financial ship  and is the founder of all knowledge to  whom we refer on occasions and  and frankly she knows from other  meetings that i've had with her  i constantly repeat my appreciation to  her although i know  the portfolio holder officially does  that but actually when you read this  report it is a tribute to all  officers senior officers in particular  but actually all officers  for the way that they manage their  directorates and  the tough times that we have and i'm  actually going to read  the first paragraph of this report  because i think  it's appropriate to place that on record  and  actually read 2.1 the financial impact  of kobit 19 has been an evolving picture  throughout 2021  and this uncertainty will continue into  2021  to 2022. managing the 2020-21 budget has  been  significantly more challenging than  usual due to the ongoing impacts of  covid19 on the council's finances  staff residents and the local economy  the council has played a significant  role in responding to the pandemic  supporting businesses and the most  vulnerable in our communities  as well as continuing to provide  essential services to all residents  furthermore what we were able to do in  this year's budget  was continue to invest in our community  investing in our car parks  investing in community safety investing  in our town centres in terms of  making them fit for the return to life  in normality so it is a huge tribute  to officers and to members  particularly the executive for the way  they steer their various portfolios  in conjunction with senior officers so i  do actually want to pay my tribute  in that way before i turn to the  recommendations any further comments  no okay i'm going to take these in in  groups of threes and fours as there's 10  uh recommendations so if you turn to  paragraphs 1.1 to 1.10  the first recommendation is to note the  provisional out turn position  against the 2021 revenue budget as  contained in paragraphs  2.1 to 2.9 is that noted members  noted  1.2 to note that the council's 2020  2020 to 21 statement of accounts are  still being prepared  and will be subject to audit by the  external auditors  student young it is therefore possible  that changes will be made to the  financial out turn  which should could alter the position  presented within this report is that  noted members  now it is and 1.3 is to approve the  transfer  to the business rate smoothing reserves  of 3071 pound  three point oh here we go three million  seventy one thousand and one hundred and  fifty nine  pounds set out in paragraph 2.9  the non-service specific expenditure  approved  yes could i have a show of hands please  and that is clearly unanimous  i must look to see where the commas are  in the long numbers must not so  i get the millions right  right moving on to um  1.4 to note the detailed breakdown of  each portfolio's  provisional out turn position at  appendix one  is that noted members  to note the detailed breakdown of  in-year reserve  movements at appendix 2 is that noted  to note the projected earmarked reserves  closing balance  at the 31st of march 2021  as set out in appendix 3 which includes  the impact  of items 1.7 to 1.8  below is that noted members  [Music]  to approve 1 million 422  909 pounds of revenue carried  carry forwards comprised of one million  one hundred and eighty four thousand one  hundred and twenty  pounds of grant budgets and  two hundred and thirty eight thousand  seven hundred and ninety pounds of  general budgets  as set out in appendix 4a and 4b  and i guess on 1.7 we have to have a  show of hands so  can i have a show of hands to approve it  and that again is unanimous  moving on to 1.8 to note the code  19 grants position detailed at appendix  4c  including ring fenced amounts to be  rolled forward  into 2021 to 2022  is that noted members noted  1.9 to note the provisional out turn  position  against the 2020 21 capital budget  as contained in paragraphs 2.12  and 213 and detailed in appendix 5.  is that noted members noted  thank you and finally 1.10  to approve 496  183 pounds of capital project  carry forwards for those schemes deemed  outstanding  at the end of 2020 to 21  into 2021 22  for completion as detailed in appendix 6  and again can i have a show of hands  please to approve that  unanimous  so members at um  7 47 p.m that actually concludes  the business of the evening so thank you  very much indeed for  to everyone for attending thank you

